  "text": "We used neatlogs to look inside every run. Each run is one trace: every probe, every model call, every guard decision, labelled by agent. On the Crustdata run, the trace shows the probe for one disputed claim. Its prediction is logged, with its hash, before the call is made. The result came back inconclusive, so Notary resolved it the safe way: it abstained, and no payment can depend on that claim. Two more mismatches, lookups that error where the docs promise an empty result, are still open. Notary hasn't certified them, so the Guard won't let money depend on them either. On the Dodo run, the trace shows the Adversary narrowing four beliefs instead of upholding them as written. Wallet credits, for example, are in minor units only for US dollars. Notary resolved those by certifying only the narrower scope it had proven.",
